      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "ARISTOPOLOS (1) was unbeaten in 6 starts as a juvenile, including 2 at stakes level, and he resumes after winning each of his 2 tune-up trials very easily. He has not reached his ceiling yet, and despite having to shoulder 60kg fresh up, he could be just too good again. ALMOST AN ANGEL (5) has been racing in good fields in Victoria, if not quite up to the stakes company on the mainland. It is a long way to travel, so her stable must think she is going well enough, and from a good draw, she is worth including in all top 3 combos. VALLEY STAR (2) is a very progressive 3YO gelding who was beaten only by a nose fresh up at Hobart just over a fortnight ago. Craig Newitt will replace an apprentice, and he should go close again. BUZZOFFSKI (4) held off the third pick when leading all the way to score last start, and she has won over this trip in the past. She will again take some pegging back. KING CANDY (3) got the job done in maiden company as the favourite last start. Include.",
